I closed the two issues this session's commits fixed, each with a comment explaining the fix. Both fixes are committed locally but not pushed yet: main is 5 commits ahead of origin/main, and the session wrap-up pushes them.

• #1057 (closed): the hourly cleanup no longer deletes the folder of a `/spawn --bg` worker that is still running. Fixed in 8616ed57.
  • Each --bg worker's entry now records its worktree (its working folder), and the cleanup skips any worktree whose worker is still marked as running.
  • I broke the check on purpose and three tests failed, then restored it in the same command.
  • Two gaps are left and are tracked in #1097, which I filed this session: workers started by another yoyo process aren't visible to the cleanup, and the folder's last-modified time still doesn't show whether a worker is active.
• #1062 (closed): a key passed with `--api-key` now skips the first-run setup wizard. Fixed in e285c907; the issue's other half (the 401 error hint) was fixed earlier in 9eff971c.
  • The tests cover all three places a key can come from (command line, environment variable, config file), plus the case with no key anywhere, which still opens the wizard.
  • On the real binary with a fresh home directory and no key variables set, --api-key dummy went straight to the prompt; the same command without the flag still showed the wizard.

